9, 11, 17, 2546, 3374, 310, 671, 20829, 681, 448, 6212, 54322, 35957, 198, 310, 421, 1850, 6479, 374, 2240, 476, 1482, 1710, 861, 1850, 1710, 510, 394, 421, 1482, 1710, 861, 435, 476, 2595, 7829, 7829, 368, 366, 2595, 13754, 1188, 3231, 1710, 481, 435, 5620, 34558, 982, 503, 1850, 6479, 284, 320, 931, 3212, 11, 501, 4178, 11, 1482, 1710, 340, 3374, 310, 421, 1850, 6479, 374, 537, 2240, 510, 394, 25362, 989, 60, 284, 1850, 6479, 7213, 262, 470, 25362, 198, 13874, 19324, 1986, 2038, 2504, 18653, 279, 1565, 4748, 666, 74263, 63, 729, 892, 5169, 264, 45736, 85897, 6132, 12111, 311, 3769, 220, 17, 21, 25362, 304, 264, 4982, 9334, 13, 576, 11900, 72, 525, 17271, 26618, 2878, 279, 14262, 315, 279, 4982, 9334, 11, 323, 1221, 5367, 7887, 12944, 1526, 18212, 9048, 804, 32587, 553, 279, 6212, 54322, 35957, 13, 1096, 5486, 21538, 311, 34508, 279, 2629, 315, 279, 12671, 11900, 72, 1393, 22573, 902, 27248, 1948, 1105, 13], "created_at": "2026-10-28T12:07:42.538342337Z", "done": true, "done_reason": "stop", "eval_count": 884, "eval_duration": 172680898689, "load_duration": 198782947, "model": "qwen2.5:3b", "prompt_eval_count": 1132, "prompt_eval_duration": 52329872691, "response": "```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.stats import qmc\n\ndef pack_circles(n: int) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Pack n circles in a unit square to maximize sum of radii.\n    \n    Args:\n        n: Number of circles to pack\n    \n    Returns:\n        Numpy array of shape (n, 3) where each row is (x, y, radius)\n        All values should be between 0 and 1\n        Circles must not overlap\n        \n    Important: Set \"all\" random seeds to 2025, including the packages (such as scipy sub-packages) involving random seeds.\n    \"\"\"\n    np.random.seed(2025)\n    if n == 0:\n        return np.zeros((0, 3))\n    \n    # Sobol sequence initialization\n    sampler = qmc.Sobol(d=2, seed=2025)\n    points = sampler.random(n)\n    circles = np.zeros((n, 3))\n    circles[:, :2] = points\n    \n    # Initial placement with random radii and positions within the unit square\n    circles[:, 2] = (np.minimum(circles[:, 0], 1 - circles[:, 0]) * \n                     np.minimum(circles[:, 1], 1 - circles[:, 1])) * 0.2 + 0.05\n    \n    # Simulated annealing with exponential cooling\n    for iteration in range(40000):\n        temperature = 0.5 * np.exp(-iteration / 10000)\n        cauchy_prob = max(0.05, 0.2 - iteration / 20000)\n        \n        for i in range(n):\n            x, y, r = circles[i]\n            \n            # Radius expansion\n            max_r = min(x, 1-x, y, 1-y)\n            for j in range(n):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                dist = np.sqrt((circles[j,0]-x)**2 + (circles[j,1]-y)**2)\n                max_r = min(max_r, dist - circles[j,2])\n            \n            best_pos = None\n            best_r = 0\n            \n            # Randomly choose a circle to perturb and try new positions\n            if np.random.random() < cauchy_prob:\n                step_size = 0.3 * temperature\n                new_x = np.clip(x + np.random.normal(0, step_size) * np.random.standard_cauchy(), 0, 1)\n                new_y = np.clip(y + np.random.normal(0, step_size) * np.random.standard_cauchy(), 0, 1)\n            else:\n                step_size = 0.04 * (1 - iteration/40000)**2\n                new_x = np.clip(x + np.random.uniform(-step_size, step_size), 0, 1)\n                new_y = np.clip(y + np.random.uniform(-step_size, step_size), 0, 1)\n            \n            current_r = min(new_x, 1-new_x, new_y, 1-new_y)\n            for j in range(n):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                dist = np.sqrt((circles[j,0]-new_x)**2 + (circles[j,1]-new_y)**2)\n                current_r = min(current_r, dist - circles[j,2])\n            \n            # Acceptance with Metropolis criterion\n            if best_pos is None or current_r > best_r:\n                if current_r > r or np.random.random() < np.exp((current_r - r)/temperature):\n                    best_pos = (new_x, new_y, current_r)\n            \n            if best_pos is not None:\n                circles[i] = best_pos\n    \n    return circles\n```\n\nThis code block defines the `pack_circles` function which implements a simulated annealing algorithm to pack 26 circles in a unit square. The radii are initialized randomly within the bounds of the unit square, and then iteratively improved through perturbations guided by the Metropolis criterion. This approach aims to maximize the sum of the circle radii while ensuring no overlap between them.", "total_duration": 227740892903}}, "revisionId": "regional-prompt-comparison-20261028", "schemaVersion": 1, "timestampUtc": "2026-10-28T12:07:42.549386+00:00"}